<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Congal Cáech</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/637">637</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Congal Cáech was king of the Dál nAraidi and of Ulaid in north-eastern Ireland, and is said to have claimed the high kingship of Tara. Allied with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/domnall-brecc">Domnall Brecc</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dal-riata">Dál Riata</a>, he fought the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ui-neill">Uí Néill</a> high king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/domnall-mac-aedo">Domnall mac Áedo</a> and was killed at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-moira">Battle of Mag Rath</a> in 637.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Domnall Brecc joined <b>Congal Cáech</b> of the Ulaid in his war against the Irish high king and was defeated at the Battle of Mag Rath in 637, which weakened Dál Riata’s position in Ireland; he was killed fighting the Britons of Strathclyde at Strathcarron in 642.</blockquote><a href="/empire/dal-riata">Dal Riata · Military</a></li><li><blockquote><b>Congal Cáech</b>, king of the Ulaid and briefly claimant to the kingship of Tara, allied with Dál Riata but was defeated and killed by Domnall mac Áedo at Mag Rath in 637.</blockquote><a href="/state/dal-naraidi">Dal nAraidi</a></li><li><blockquote>Kings such as Báetán mac Cairill and <b>Congal Cáech</b> challenged the Uí Néill, but defeat at Mag Rath in 637 ended their hopes of wider supremacy.</blockquote><a href="/state/kingdom-of-ulaid">Kingdom of Ulaid</a></li></ul></section>
